> The problem we're having is that if we send more than about 5 at a
> time to the printer, the images are scrambled. 

I am not quite sure if the HPdeskjet 1200 as its LaserJet brothers send messages
back to the host (beside XON/XOFF), but if this is the case this is the problem because
HP Laserjet printers are not supported by LATSYM at this time. To try if this is your
problem you should create a queue with no latsym processor:

	$ stop/queu/reset queuename
	$ init/queue/noprocessor queuename
	$ start/queue queue name

Now test again, if every thing prints fine now, the above mentioned problem is yours.
Now you may continue to use your printer without LATSYM which is also not supported
(but anyway), but remember then that once your queu is started it will keep your LAT
connection to the printer up all the time preventing any other host from accessing that
printer over LAT.

Gast.




